#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/id #uuid "a2b50673-6a4f-5e64-ae16-fdce0819637e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8526" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.1450$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1469 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1446 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1423 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1711 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1685 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1660 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1977 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1949 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1922 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1450$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1446$ and $0.1469.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1446 & <0.1450<0.1469\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\\Phi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.06) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.05).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz \\approx \\dfrac{-1.06 + (-1.05)}{2} = -1.055.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166596 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "d1e64fae-04ef-5c7d-9bb0-e81cf06bb672" :question/math-academy-id "e-8528" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.60.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.60$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.2533\\,$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $\\Phi{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.60 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz = \\Phi^{-1} (0.60).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p = 0.60,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np = 0.60 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}(p) = 0.2533.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz =  \\Phi^{-1}(0.60) = 0.2533.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "a29f1f2c-104a-53aa-ad55-0c6abde0a359" :question/math-academy-id "e-8590" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.20.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\leq 0.8416 ) = 0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\geq 0.8416 ) = 1 - 0.80 = 0.20.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-0.8416) = 0.20.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/2be6ef2420c8789a0ff94f4f9540533af4134690ebe0c04c50eb02f358dfa266.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.8416) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le -0.8416) & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required value of $z$ is $-0.8416.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a969516e-2b4e-590e-8d41-4f928bbfa55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.235" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366506} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3503f6-1b82-5773-8902-218c6e4b3467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366507} {:answer/id #uuid "299c8916-ce94-5aac-bff7-aeebc6465bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366508} {:answer/id #uuid "03ac4d3c-d194-5aab-8faf-1132496a6212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.265" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366509} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ea7916-392e-5d85-bb9e-5bc1e326f557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.145" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b3503f6-1b82-5773-8902-218c6e4b3467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366507} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b478aa9-837f-53b9-beaf-fb8d4bb6e9e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fcd13a72-8b86-535f-8810-8ff4425a5648" :question/math-academy-id "q-164175" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.1060$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0901\\,$ | $\\,0.0885\\,$ | $\\,0.0869\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1075\\,$ | $\\,0.1056\\,$ | $\\,0.1038\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1271\\,$ | $\\,0.1251\\,$ | $\\,0.1230\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1060$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1056$ and $0.1075.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1056 & <0.1060<0.1075\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.25) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.24).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-1.25+(-1.24)}{2}=-1.245.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1453594-8903-50ee-b9d7-f8aaabacf704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366513} {:answer/id #uuid "39444dad-fcaa-5499-b889-e665714443a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366514} {:answer/id #uuid "7adec1a6-f7ae-5c33-a0b8-26e45c386e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366515} {:answer/id #uuid "d381e7bc-2315-5e0e-b25a-31aa654af2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366516} {:answer/id #uuid "06d9958a-f340-5897-a021-a36f063f9008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d381e7bc-2315-5e0e-b25a-31aa654af2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366516} :answer-field/id #uuid "5269a913-7768-5a04-9570-e3fb0a25f68f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a7797ab7-1899-58d2-99c9-ce6561ce19c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-164333" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.01.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.99\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.99,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.99\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.3263.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99)=2.3263.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2bd46cd-9a77-513c-8356-8210f01ffdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.625" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366520} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e4d3bb-d3e2-5456-bf38-a8ebbef06833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.525" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2bd46cd-9a77-513c-8356-8210f01ffdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.625" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366520} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1486ffd-9d97-5863-a027-6ed7bbca62f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab06af99-e963-57ee-8889-5cc42add1bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-328306" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9564\\,$ | $\\,0.9573\\,$ | $\\,0.9582\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9480$ using interval bisection and the above table.\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.9480$ lies between. These numbers are $0.9474$ and $0.9484.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9474 & <0.9480<0.9484\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.62) & <Φ(z)<Φ(1.63).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{1.62+1.63}{2}=1.625.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89679406-aa4b-5f06-b387-30555b81492b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.325" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366524} {:answer/id #uuid "e12b9615-8b76-5198-9aec-bd4a84e12f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.325" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e12b9615-8b76-5198-9aec-bd4a84e12f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.325" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366525} :answer-field/id #uuid "339537be-aceb-5a31-b2a7-892d6dd7394d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cc7a771-75d4-545c-8237-deaeb107f4db" :question/math-academy-id "q-328313" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ | $\\,0.3669\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ | $\\,0.4090\\,$ | $\\,0.4052\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ | $\\,0.4483\\,$ | $\\,0.4443\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.3725$ using interval bisection and the above table\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.3725$ lies between. These numbers are $0.3707$ and $0.3745.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.3707 & <0.3725<0.3745\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.33) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-0.32).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-0.33+(-0.32)}{2}=-0.325.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29990dc9-7c47-5a7d-a683-f305a4820df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366528} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a00f91-a433-555e-a322-b039e7668011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29990dc9-7c47-5a7d-a683-f305a4820df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366528} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d482933-24a2-5616-8b42-c4cf8860f69c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1968863c-3f80-51a3-b4be-3ffbe2b32d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-328454" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.90.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.90 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.90).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.90,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.90\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=1.2816.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.90)=1.2816.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71576a10-60ec-5fd1-8b2e-fb397ead9e28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3853" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366532} {:answer/id #uuid "a55d370e-ccbb-5b81-80a3-228987379a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ